  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Lfu &#x2013; Norwegian Veterinary Institute - Capacity development One Health &#x2013; Implementation</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Impact 
Sustainable production of safe milk that contributes to food security, improved nutrition, increased animal and human health as well as economic growth.

Outcome 1 &#x2013; Operational One Health Platforms for coordinated control of zoonoses and AMR in the milk value chain
Outcome 2 &#x2013; Capacity for surveillance of AMR, antimicrobial use and infectious diseases in the milk value chain
Outcome 3 &#x2013; Capacity to detect zoonotic diseases through laboratory investigations
Outcome 4 &#x2013; Veterinary services surrounding primary producers of the milk value chain has been established in selected countries and regions

Target groups: 
a) Veterinary authorities in Malawi and Ethiopia
-Government and civil society stakeholders involved in control of zoonotic disease on the side of public health and animal health
-Government employees involved in surveillance of zoonotic diseases &#x2013; animal- and public health. 
-Government laboratory personnel of at least one national reference laboratory for animal health and one national reference laboratory for public health, as well as 2-4 regional reference laboratories for each sector. In addition to train a certain number of animal health professionals at regional level for sampling and results-interpretation. 

b)  Dairy farmers in Malawi and Ethiopia
In Malawi, the veterinary services surrounding the 36 milk collection points associated with Lilongwe dairy have been suggested. For Ethiopia this remains to be clarified.</narrative>
  </description>
